# TypeScript

## Type System - Co-located Types

Types live next to the code that uses them. Only truly shared types remain in `/src/lib/types/`.

### Type Locations
- `$lib/models/types.ts` / `typeGuards.ts` - Model types and guards
- `$lib/components/chat-history/types.ts` / `typeGuards.ts` - Chat/message types and guards
- `$lib/db/types.ts` - Database and user types
- `$lib/services/llm/types.ts` - LLM provider types (incl. provider image formats)
- `$lib/services/llm/tool-types.ts` - LLM tool types
- `$lib/services/stripe/types.ts` - Stripe payment types
- `$lib/types/attachment.ts` - Shared attachment types (`Image`, `FileAttachment`)
- `$lib/types/customErrors.ts` - Custom error classes

### Rules
1. Co-locate types with usage — don't add to `/src/lib/types/` unless used across 3+ domains
2. Check existing co-located files before creating new types
3. Always use explicit type annotations (variables, params, return types)
4. Use `unknown` over `any`, then narrow with type guards
5. Import Prisma enums/types directly from `@prisma/client`
6. Use SvelteKit's `$types` for page/layout types


## Type Safety

- Strict mode enabled in `tsconfig.json`
- Run `npm run check` to validate
- CI/CD fails on type errors
